-## Observation, inference, unknown
-
-**Observed**: the four carriers hash to the pins; the superblock fields in the table; every member
-digest and size in the census; the equality of the two byte orders' member censuses; the
-`unsquashfs -s` lines; the `file` labels; `7z l` listing all four carriers; the 0x78da stream
-offsets; the v2ns refusals from both external readers and its two-byte magic diff; the `7z`
-listing of the LE broadcom fixture; the handler classes, patterns, `EXTRACTOR` and the argv
-decision at the cited lines; and the scored counter's fields quoted above (`carriers_matched 4/4`,
-`met_target true`, `failing []`, `per_carrier_failing` empty, `gap_kinds []`, `coverage complete`).
-
-**Inferred** (derived, not measured): the v2 `block_size_1` of 0 is the 16-bit truncation of
-65536 (arithmetic, cross-checked against the reader's printed block size); the `file` word is a
-layout artifact (it flips with byte order while the `flags` byte and every member digest stay the
-same); these four carriers exercise only the regular-file publication path (their census holds no
-symlink, device node or second directory level).
-
-**Unknown**: what bit `0x40` of the v1/v2 `flags` byte means; whether any SquashFS v1/v2 image
-outside these four extracts through REA at all; and which process wrote the committed receipts —
-the counter's rerun projection bounds a fabricated envelope but cannot attest who ran the origin
-run (R40-CL2).
